<p>LOOKING AHEAD →</p>
<p>Chapter 1 ended with a rough first statement of the moral law: act only on maxims you could will to be universal. Chapter 2 is where Kant develops this into the famous categorical imperative, gives it multiple formulations, and applies it to specific cases. It is the central chapter of the book.</p>
